WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.250
- Unlike the first two movies,

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:02.580
the third Conjuring doesn't begin

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.350
with a cold open showing us another case

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:05.940
from the history of Ed
and Lorraine Warren,

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.740
but that doesn't mean the
opening doesn't reference

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.240
another well known exorcism.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:10.600
The entire style of the open,

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.670
in particular the shots

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.210
of Father Gordon arriving at the house,

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:15.460
pay tribute to the iconic
shots of Father Merrin

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.590
from The Exorcist, an image also featured

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:19.090
on The Exorcist movie poster.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:20.320
The way that David Glatzel,

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.500
the young boy who is possessed,

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.590
moves and convulses is very reminiscent

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.440
of what happens to
Regan in The Exorcist.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.240
Obviously The Exorcist
kind of set the stage

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.190
for an entire genre of exorcism movies,

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:30.800
which includes the original Conjuring,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.810
which I've already analyzed
on Things You Missed.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:33.740
But the reason this third

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.980
installment references
the 1973 horror film

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.590
so heavily may be because
The Exorcist movie itself

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:40.030
could have influenced the real version

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:42.350
of the allegedly possessed
killer, Arne Johnson.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:45.370
In 1981, the cultural impact
of the film was still fresh

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.530
and Satanic panic was
on the rise in the 80s.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.050
According to the New York Times,

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:51.130
Debbie Glatzel had
watched The Exorcist on TV

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.920
with her family and attended at least one

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.070
of the Warrens' lectures
before her brother began

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:56.410
to claim his visions of the devil.

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.150
So William Friedkin's famous movie

00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:01.120
may have actually influenced
the entire chain of events.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.160
To learn about all of the secret details

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:05.270
that reference both the
greater Conjuring universe

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:08.110
and real events upon which the
fictional story was inspired,

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.902
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:10.902 --> 00:01:13.652
(dramatic music)

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:17.860
Like that new intro?

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.350
Welcome to Things You Missed.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.340
The name of this movie

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:22.420
is The Conjuring: The Devil Made Me Do It.

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:24.460
However, I don't wanna say
that long title every time,

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:26.270
so I'll be calling it The Conjuring 3,

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:27.650
and before you send your death threats

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:28.720
over me calling it that,

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.920
keep in mind that James
Wan even called it that.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.550
So, if you're gonna kill me,
gonna have to take him out too.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:36.200
However, James Wan was not
the director of this movie.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:37.960
It would instead be Michael Chaves,

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.140
who directed The Curse of La Llorona.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:42.155
Let's get into the Things You Missed.

00:01:42.155 --> 00:01:44.738
(upbeat music)

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:49.240
Once again, the main character drama

00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:50.600
for the Warrens involves them getting

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.570
into danger by being involved in the case.

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:54.940
This time, Ed starts to
experience heart problems.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.030
In the movie, we see that this
heart condition is a result

00:01:57.030 --> 00:01:58.390
of an attack by the demon itself.

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:01.140
DEMON: I'll stop your heart old man!

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.120
- The real Ed Warren
did have a heart attack,

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.350
supposedly he had several
in his later years,

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:07.570
but it wasn't during this
case and it obviously

00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:09.980
wasn't related to demonic
activity, but rather,

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:13.440
probably related to a
lifestyle of unhealthy choices.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.960
- LORRAINE: Somebody call 911!

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:16.140
- You're not supposed to do that Lorraine,

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:17.547
you're supposed to point
at someone and say,

00:02:17.547 --> 00:02:19.360
"You, call 911."

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.940
Otherwise everyone assumes
someone else will do it.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:23.700
After the hysteria calms down a bit,

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:24.800
we're introduced to the house

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:25.960
where the crime would take place

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:27.620
in a long, continuous shot.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.740
This is how we were introduced
to the Old Arnold Estate

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:30.670
in The Conjuring 1,

00:02:30.670 --> 00:02:32.600
and the house in The Curse of La Llorona

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:33.920
although, in The Conjuring 3,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.600
it's more symbolic of just carrying

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.090
on the tradition than anything else.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.590
In The Conjuring, it was the perfect way

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:40.290
to teach the audience
the layout of the house

00:02:40.290 --> 00:02:41.910
where we'd be spending most of the movie.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.080
And three, we don't really
go back to that house,

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.350
so it's more for show.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.310
There's another familiar
piece of camera work later

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.080
in the movie where we
see the Satanic ritual

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.250
being performed, and the
camera flips upside-down

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.890
to signify the presence of evil,

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.570
just like it does as Lorraine enters

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.850
and exits the basement
where Bathsheba is located

00:02:56.850 --> 00:02:57.920
in The Conjuring 1.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:59.960
Arne helps his girlfriend's
boss fix his stereo,

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.370
and in the background there's a poster

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:03.850
for Mack the Knife, which
would be a foreshadowing

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.170
of what could happen next.

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:07.000
As Saul dances to this Blondie song,

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.910
Arne has a vision where, for a moment,

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:09.743
it looks like Debbie

00:03:09.743 --> 00:03:11.320
is dancing up against her boss.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:13.370
This is kind of a quick
reference to an aspect

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:14.520
of the real life event.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.240
According to the Pensacola News Journal,

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.030
the police believed that
Debbie and her boss,

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.540
whose real name is Alan Bono,

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.430
may have had a romantic relationship,

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.610
and that the argument may not
have been about the stereo,

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.810
but that they were actually
quarreling over Debbie,

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.290
and things escalated because
alcohol was involved.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.370
Though I can't say I
understand how the police

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:31.740
would have come to that conclusion.

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:32.990
We see Arne's point of view,

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.960
where he sees this evil
entity rushing him.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:37.300
At first, it has the sharp
white specs for eyes,

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.560
much like we see on Janice
in Annabelle Creation,

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:40.610
but as it gets closer it

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:42.670
has the unnatural yellow glow similar

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:44.480
to Valak's eyes in The Conjuring 2.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.530
I think this is done to kind

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.310
of honor the history of the franchise.

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:48.920
We don't actually see
the crime take place,

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:50.860
which plays nicely with the idea that even

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:51.760
in The Conjurverse,

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.570
where the paranormal clearly exists,

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:55.810
there are always going to
be believers and skeptics.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:57.510
The victim also still
has living relatives,

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:58.890
so changing the character's name

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:00.120
and not showing the knife go in

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:03.000
is probably at least a little
bit of a respectful move.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.080
After Arne's arrest,

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.290
the Warrens perform these tests

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:07.130
to see if he's housing an inhuman spirit.

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:09.700
I'm not sure why they're so
confident that this will work.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:11.850
You'd think they might remember
the tests they performed

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.090
in The Conjuring 2, three
and a half years ago.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.520
Speaking of things that
haven't always been consistent,

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.290
let's talk about the Warrens' house.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:19.630
In the first film we only really see the

00:04:19.630 --> 00:04:21.270
areas connected to the stair hallway

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:22.387
with the flower wallpaper.

00:04:22.387 --> 00:04:23.940
Conjuring 2 shows the office,

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:25.860
a kitchen, a living room and this study.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.710
And Annabelle Comes Home
has the same office,

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:29.300
but a different kitchen and living room,

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:30.530
and it's here that we learn the layout

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:31.697
of the rest of the house.

00:04:31.697 --> 00:04:33.730
Conjuring 3 seems to use the same layout.

00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:35.970
This is the dining room where
Judy held her birthday party.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:37.700
Those are the stairs
up towards Judy's room.

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:39.850
Ed wakes up in the room where
Judy encountered the ghost

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:40.683
of the wedding dress.

00:04:40.683 --> 00:04:43.160
So considering that the
timeline looks like this,

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.580
it's now clear that the house used

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.210
in Annabelle Comes Home was a retcon,

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:48.650
as opposed to the idea that
they remodeled after that,

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:50.810
but at least we have a
consistent layout going forward.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.920
Goodbye, mysterious room that
isn't connected to anything.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.770
The Warrens listen back
to their audio interviews

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:56.603
of the family,

00:04:56.603 --> 00:04:58.250
and we see a flashback
to the day they moved

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.930
into the house and they're unloading boxes

00:04:59.930 --> 00:05:01.710
from a Saunders Moving Company truck.

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:02.870
This is a sneaky reference

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.540
to the travel co-ordinator of the movie,

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:05.810
Ashley Renee Saunders.

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.500
I cover crew reference
easter eggs like this

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.380
in nearly every episode
of Things You Missed,

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.510
but putting the travel
co-ordinator on a moving truck

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.890
has gotta be one of the most
creative ones I've seen.

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:15.960
I've also covered a lot
of James Wan movies,

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:18.330
and talked about how moving
is a common theme for him,

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:19.640
it happens in The Conjuring,

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.870
Dead Silence and twice in Insidious.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:22.703
As I mentioned,

00:05:22.703 --> 00:05:24.750
The Conjuring 3 wasn't
directed by James Wan,

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:26.180
but I think it's still worth noting

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.600
because Michael Chaves is trying

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.170
to emulate his style with this.

00:05:29.170 --> 00:05:30.980
But Chaves is also his own person,

00:05:30.980 --> 00:05:32.730
with his own personal influences.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.070
As Lorraine investigates the house,

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:36.440
she pulls out a camera to get
some photographic evidence,

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.700
and this is the camera
used by Carl Kolchak

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.820
in the 1974 The Night Stalker.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.960
I'm guessing Chaves is probably a fan.

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:43.990
But the biggest connection

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:45.920
in The Conjuring 3 gives us more insight

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:49.585
to one big mystery left open
in the Annabelle spin-offs.

00:05:49.585 --> 00:05:52.085
(tense music)

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:57.620
(upbeat soft music)

00:06:06.639 --> 00:06:09.639
(suspenseful music)

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:46.553
(screaming)

00:06:53.897 --> 00:06:56.500
Desperate for leads about
their discovery of the witch's

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:57.560
totem under the house,

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.530
Father Gordon has a suggestion about where

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:00.660
to look next.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:03.230
- Do you remember the priest
who helped expose The Disciples

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:04.700
of the Ram cult?

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:06.790
It would have been about 10-12 years ago?

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:09.330
- If you've seen my episodes
covering the Annabelle movies,

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:11.080
all about The Disciples of Ram.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:12.450
It's explained on a TV playing

00:07:12.450 --> 00:07:14.057
in the background in Annabelle 1 that they

00:07:14.057 --> 00:07:15.910
are a Charles Manson led cult looking

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:17.630
to make ritual sacrifices in hopes

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:18.700
of summoning a demon.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:20.550
We know that two of these
cult members pass away

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:22.360
after successfully completing the ritual,

00:07:22.360 --> 00:07:24.270
and we know that the
demon ends up eventually

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.600
being sealed away in the
Warren's cursed artifact room,

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:28.530
but we never learned what
happened to the other members

00:07:28.530 --> 00:07:31.300
of the cult until now: Father
Kastner tried to help them,

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:32.230
but was unable to,

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:34.370
because their sole aim
was to spread chaos.

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:36.040
There's also a more salient reference

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:37.110
to The Conjuring 1.

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:38.133
Roll it.

00:07:40.347 --> 00:07:42.140
- LORRAINE: You should burn all this.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:43.140
- KASTNER: I'd thought of it.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:47.407
But I felt it was safer
to keep them locked.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:50.730
Like taking guns off the streets.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:53.160
- I don't understand why Lorraine
doesn't know that already,

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:55.840
because these are literally
the same words that Ed used

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.700
to explain the danger of cursed objects

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:59.590
to a reporter.

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:02.400
- It's safer for these things
to be in here than out there.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.200
It's kind of like keeping
guns off the street.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:06.910
- Well why not just throw
them in an incinerator?

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:07.743
Destroy them?

00:08:07.743 --> 00:08:09.030
- Well that would only destroy the vessel.

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.970
- Maybe witch objects don't work the same

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:12.540
as cursed vessels?

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.320
You'd think Lorraine
would be on top of this.

00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.040
You'd also think Ed would be smart enough

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:19.440
to follow his own advice and
not touch one of the objects.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.980
- ED: Don't touch it.

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:23.510
- Ed ends up being controlled
by this demon himself later

00:08:23.510 --> 00:08:24.343
in the movie,

00:08:24.343 --> 00:08:25.176
but Lorraine does not,

00:08:25.176 --> 00:08:26.590
so I wonder if touching that book

00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:28.080
is what ended up making him vulnerable.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:29.870
- Ed, don't.

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:32.080
- Then there's this idol
seen on a bookshelf.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:33.530
It may look kind of like Malthus,

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.830
but it's wings make it
more similar to Baphomet,

00:08:35.830 --> 00:08:37.590
a deity worshipped by the Knights Templar

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:39.560
that was active starting
in the 12th century.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:41.650
Baphomet may be another mythological demon

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:43.070
that the creators could explore

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:44.950
in a future Conjuring universe film.

00:08:44.950 --> 00:08:47.320
There are a lot of other
options introduced as well,

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:48.900
as the gang is trying to figure out who

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:51.330
or what this demon that
possessed Arne actually is

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.880
and list all of their options
on this big chalkboard.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:55.890
We can only really see the
left side of the board,

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:57.100
which lists the clues they found

00:08:57.100 --> 00:08:58.680
from Father Kastner's collection.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.540
Some of these seem to
be just made up words,

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:02.450
while others are more specific references.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:04.730
We'd be here for a while if
I went through all of them,

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:06.410
but you can pause as we go if you want,

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:08.050
and I'll just list the ones I could see

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:09.190
maybe being the subject

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.880
of a future Conjuring spin-off movie.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:11.713
But just to be clear,

00:09:11.713 --> 00:09:13.160
I don't think these items are listed here

00:09:13.160 --> 00:09:15.150
as a specific clue for some future movie,

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:16.780
this is obviously just set decoration

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:18.930
that we're not really
supposed to pause and read,

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:21.140
but it's just nice to know
what's on their radar I guess,

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:22.350
so let's go through them.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:23.183
The Fallen.

00:09:23.183 --> 00:09:24.360
Apostasy of the Weak.

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:25.460
Daemonium Rex.

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:26.580
Walpurgisnacht.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:28.220
Rituals of Roanoke Witches.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:29.053
Yellow King.

00:09:29.053 --> 00:09:30.310
Abaddon Amas.

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:31.143
Balaam.

00:09:31.143 --> 00:09:32.140
Conjuring of Ishtar.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:33.170
Kali Mamoon.

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.970
I will not attempt to pronounce this one,

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:37.630
but it refers to an Aztec
god of night and sorcery.

00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.500
Again, none of these
are concrete references

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.660
to anything previously
appearing in the Conjurverse,

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:43.240
I just thought it would
be fun to explore some

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:45.210
of the avenues that the
Warrens might have researched

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:46.043
in this movie.

00:09:46.043 --> 00:09:47.500
If you want more of a concrete reference,

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:48.520
you can find one when Ed

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:49.500
and Lorraine return home

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:51.950
after visiting Father
Kastner's own artifact room.

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:52.783
Roll it.

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:57.063
- LORRAINE: Look what
the Perron Family sent.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:01.000
- ED: Oh, that was sweet of them.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:01.833
- The Perron Family,

00:10:01.833 --> 00:10:03.430
is of course the family that Ed

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:05.780
and Lorraine helped save in
the original Conjuring film.

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:06.613
So it's nice to see

00:10:06.613 --> 00:10:08.290
that they've kept in
touch for a decade now

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:09.123
in the movies.

00:10:09.123 --> 00:10:11.300
Because if you've seen
my Conjuring 1 episode,

00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:14.030
that they didn't exactly stay
on good terms in real life.

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:16.060
There's also a nice little
detail on the fridge.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:17.170
In Annabelle Comes Home,

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:18.390
Lorraine expresses a desire

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:21.018
to take a road trip out
West with the family.

00:10:21.018 --> 00:10:23.062
- That actually sounds so nice.

00:10:23.062 --> 00:10:24.350
Ed, we should plan on that.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:26.340
- Based on this family
photo, which was not there

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:27.210
in Annabelle Comes Home,

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:29.400
it looks like they probably
did take that trip.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.790
The Warrens end up going on
a side-quest to track down

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:33.410
this missing girl, Jessica Strong,

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:36.000
which leads them to visit the
town of Danvers, Massachusets.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.040
In the car, the song
"Suspicious Minds" comes

00:10:38.040 --> 00:10:39.560
on the radio, and Lorraine comments

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:42.790
that she actually met Elvis
both before and after his death

00:10:42.790 --> 00:10:43.860
and looks at her husband,

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:45.890
making reference to Ed's
killer Elvis impression

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:47.770
that we saw when he was
helping the Hodgson family

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.241
in The Conjuring 2.

00:10:49.241 --> 00:10:50.074
- Thank you.

00:10:50.074 --> 00:10:50.907
(children laughing)

00:10:50.907 --> 00:10:52.469
Hey don't laugh now.

00:10:52.469 --> 00:10:53.302
Thank you very much.

00:10:53.302 --> 00:10:55.700
- After Superhero Lorraine
uses her psychic abilities

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:57.130
to find out what happened to the girl,

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.250
they spend the night in the Bruneau Motel.

00:10:59.250 --> 00:11:00.950
This is another crew reference easter egg,

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:03.150
probably left there by
Eric and Ian Bruneau,

00:11:03.150 --> 00:11:04.400
the visual effects producer

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:06.130
and a technician respectively.

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:07.580
Using the information they collected,

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:10.090
they determine that
their guy Arne is cursed.

00:11:10.090 --> 00:11:13.520
- LORRAINE: That means we
know that this is a curse,

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:15.320
and curses can be broken.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:16.500
- Hell yeah, they can!

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:18.460
The couple decides to try to make contact

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:19.960
with the person who issued this curse,

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:22.140
and the best way to do this
is by visiting the body.

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:24.470
So, they arrive at the
Palmeri Funeral Home.

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:27.127
Palmeri really is a huge
empire in the Conjurverse.

00:11:27.127 --> 00:11:28.797
Annabelle had the Palmeri apartments,

00:11:28.797 --> 00:11:30.890
Annabelle Creation had
the Palmeri Toy Shop.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:31.780
And even Lights Out,

00:11:31.780 --> 00:11:33.490
which is not even part of the Conjurse,

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:35.270
but is a fellow Warner Bros horror film,

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:36.530
had Palmeri Elementary.

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:38.330
David F Sandberg, who directed Lights Out

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:39.163
and Annabelle Creation,

00:11:39.163 --> 00:11:41.370
happens to be a fellow
content creator and filled us

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:43.130
in on the meaning of
Palmeri in the comments

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:44.660
of my Annabelle Creation episode.

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:46.430
It's a reference to Victoria Palmeri

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:47.670
who works at New Line.

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:49.870
The funeral home is closed
when Ed and Lorraine arrive,

00:11:49.870 --> 00:11:52.130
so they do their best Clear
Rivers from Final Destination

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:53.950
and decide to break in.

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:54.950
- Gives me a rush.

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:56.720
- Lorraine is able to come face-to-face

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:57.870
with the occultist, Isla,

00:11:57.870 --> 00:11:59.520
or as I call her: The Malnourished Lady,

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:01.080
during one of her astral projections,

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:02.410
but Ed has to pull her out

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:05.061
when she's attacked by this evil force.

00:12:05.061 --> 00:12:08.594
(monster groans)

00:12:08.594 --> 00:12:11.344
(dramatic music)

00:12:14.397 --> 00:12:16.980
(upbeat music)

00:12:17.935 --> 00:12:19.540
Before Ed and Lorraine return home,

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:23.050
their assistant guy Drew finds
a book that might help them

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.660
because it's a Conjuring movie,

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:26.610
of course they find a
book that might help them.

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:28.410
Ed discovers that the curse can be broken

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:30.370
by destroying the altar it was cast from,

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:32.950
but isn't able to read much further.

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:34.350
- ED: This part looks like Aramaic.

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:36.730
This next part, I can't read it.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:39.580
- Aramaic is an ancient language
spoken in the Middle East,

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:41.890
which is yet another
potential tie to The Disciples

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:43.050
of Ram from Annabelle,

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:45.330
whose cult was partly based
on an ancient text found

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:47.290
on the bank of the Dead
Sea in that region.

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:50.000
I did a whole video about
Malthus, the Annabelle demon,

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:51.210
so if you're interested in learning more

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:53.520
about that connection,
definitely check that one out.

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:55.130
Given that Conjuring 3 seems to be

00:12:55.130 --> 00:12:56.680
so heavily linked to Annabelle,

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:59.060
it's kind of cool that after
Ed answers a phantom knock

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:01.080
on his door, the spot that Isla appears

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.300
is practically the same
spot that Annabelle appeared

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.400
in behind Judy's babysitter
when she answered

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:07.100
to a ghostly presence knocking at the door

00:13:07.100 --> 00:13:08.160
in Annabelle 3.

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:10.810
After nearly being manipulated
to attack his own wife,

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:13.300
Ed realizes that he
too is being influenced

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:15.620
by a witch's totem hidden
somewhere in the house

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:17.440
and goes on a mad tirade to find it.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:18.610
While searching in the office,

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:20.770
I noticed these two
paintings in the background.

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:22.840
This one looks like the
Penfield Reef lighthouse,

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:25.180
which is a supposedly haunted
lighthouse in Connecticut

00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:26.050
where the Warrens live,

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:26.990
but as far as I know,

00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:29.110
they've never actually made
an investigation into it

00:13:29.110 --> 00:13:29.943
in real life.

00:13:29.943 --> 00:13:31.730
The other painting is
the one he was working on

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:32.850
in Annabelle Comes Home.

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:34.770
I don't think it references
anything specific,

00:13:34.770 --> 00:13:37.270
but it's just a cool detail
to show that passage of time.

00:13:37.270 --> 00:13:38.103
Late that night,

00:13:38.103 --> 00:13:39.820
Lorraine goes to visit
Father Kastner again,

00:13:39.820 --> 00:13:41.800
hoping he could help
translate the foreign text,

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:43.280
and there is a very familiar scene

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:45.330
of him locking the door
behind her as she comes in,

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:46.470
leading her to the basement,

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:48.723
and creepily waiting for her in the dark.

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:52.900
- GRAYSMITH: Not many people
have basements in FAIRFIELD.

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:54.290
- Not everyone will get that reference,

00:13:54.290 --> 00:13:55.280
but I'd just like to point out

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:57.400
that both movies have a Key Largo poster.

00:13:57.400 --> 00:13:58.800
That can't be a coincidence.

00:13:59.689 --> 00:14:00.522
(bright upbeat music)

00:14:00.522 --> 00:14:02.460
So that just leaves us
with the final battle,

00:14:02.460 --> 00:14:04.630
where it seems that
Superhero Lorraine Warren

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:06.110
has finally met her match.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.820
I think it's symbolic how Isla attempts

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.200
to stab Lorraine in the eye.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.620
Lorraine's main source of strength

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:11.940
is through her psychic visions,

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:14.000
and considering how she
sees these images as sort

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:15.540
of an overlay of her literal vision,

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.110
she might not be able to have her gift

00:14:17.110 --> 00:14:18.080
without her eyes.

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:20.290
The whole Ed Warren
going after his loved one

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:22.650
with a sledgehammer part
is very The Shining,

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:23.483
where in the book,

00:14:23.483 --> 00:14:25.610
Jack Torrance chases his
son with a large mallet.

00:14:25.610 --> 00:14:27.000
But after taking care of Isla,

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.500
and freeing Ed from her control,

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:29.670
there's one more issue,

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:31.970
when Ed forgets his heart
pills and Lorraine reveals

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.320
that she kept an extra on her,

00:14:33.320 --> 00:14:35.120
hidden inside the locket on her necklace.

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:36.910
Observant fans will
notice that this is more

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:38.700
than just a sweet gesture towards, Ed.

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:40.040
This is the same locket given

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:43.020
to Lorraine by Judy ten years
before in The Conjuring 1.

00:14:43.020 --> 00:14:47.129
- JUDY: Me and Nana got these
at the church's yard sale.

00:14:47.129 --> 00:14:48.520
One for you and one for me.

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:50.920
- As always, Ed transfers
one of the cursed objects

00:14:50.920 --> 00:14:52.170
from this case, the chalice,

00:14:52.170 --> 00:14:54.470
to the Warren's occult
museum of cursed artifacts,

00:14:54.470 --> 00:14:55.360
where we see everything

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:57.120
from their past cases accounted for

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:59.140
even if some stuff has been
moved around a little bit

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:01.620
in the almost four years
since The Conjuring 2.

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:03.660
We see the music box from The Conjuring,

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:05.340
The color wheel from Annabelle Comes Home,

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:07.720
The Crooked Man Zootrope
toy from The Conjuring 2,

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.470
The Valak painting from The Conjuring 2

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:12.430
and The Annabelle doll
from obviously Annabelle,

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:14.650
The trial of Arne Johnson
ends up just being more

00:15:14.650 --> 00:15:15.483
of an epilogue.

00:15:15.483 --> 00:15:17.690
As always, the result is
a lot more fictionalized

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:18.930
for movie audiences.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.200
The reason we don't really
see any of the trial could be

00:15:21.200 --> 00:15:23.040
because Arne's lawyer
didn't ultimately end up

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.470
using the "Devil Made Him
Do It" defense in court,

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:26.630
because the judge said that

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:28.280
this defense would not be allowed.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.300
So his lawyer changed
his plea to say that it

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:31.710
was an act of self defense.

00:15:31.710 --> 00:15:34.030
The text in the movie says
Arne served five years,

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.050
which is true.

00:15:35.050 --> 00:15:36.750
He was sentenced for 10-20 years,

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:38.540
but got out early on good behavior.

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.520
The end credits use the
same slideshow style

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:41.670
from The Conjuring 2.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:42.730
Like The Conjuring 2,

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:44.760
there are some subliminal images that pop

00:15:44.760 --> 00:15:46.870
on-screen for just one or two frames.

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:48.960
One of these is an
actual newspaper article.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:51.420
I found the most interesting
part to be this paragraph,

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:53.610
Meanwhile, the parents
of the 11-year-old boy

00:15:53.610 --> 00:15:55.010
say the spirits remain.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:57.720
Another one that I found
particularly creepy was this one,

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:00.130
it appears to be Arne being
exorcized at the prison

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:02.580
and trashing about in
an almost inhumane way.

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:04.130
There's also this pretty chilling picture

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:05.690
of the malnourished lady Isla,

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.440
or at least the demon that possessed her.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:08.910
Strangely, we never really learn much

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:10.010
about the demon itself,

00:16:10.010 --> 00:16:12.350
a stark contrast to the
rich lore behind entities

00:16:12.350 --> 00:16:14.570
like Valak, Bathsheba and Malthus.

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:16.650
Then of course, there's
a shot of Annabelle,

00:16:16.650 --> 00:16:19.100
don't be surprised if we
haven't seen the last of her.

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:20.810
This last one appears
to be an illustration

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:22.200
of the real Arne Johnson.

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:24.550
You may be wondering how the
Warrens got Debbie Glatzel

00:16:24.550 --> 00:16:25.700
and her family to go along

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:27.400
with the whole demonic possession story.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:28.960
According to History vs Hollywood,

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:30.880
the brother of the 11
year old David claimed

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:32.920
that the Warrens promised
the family money and fame

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:34.700
to the tune of millions of dollars,

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:37.140
but only ended up making them about $2K.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:39.990
Of course the Warrens denied
this, there was a lawsuit.

00:16:39.990 --> 00:16:41.690
money makes the world go round.

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:43.690
I'd like to bring your
attention to the playlist

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.850
on the left which contains
Things You Missed episodes

00:16:45.850 --> 00:16:47.910
on every movie in the Conjurverse to date.

00:16:47.910 --> 00:16:49.860
And for even more Conjuring analysis,

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:51.633
make sure you're subscribed to CZsWorld.

00:16:51.633 --> 00:16:53.720
I'll be uploading new horrors every week,

00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:56.070
so ring the deathbell
for ALL notifications

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:58.070
and I'll see you in the next one.

00:16:58.070 --> 00:17:00.618
Assuming we both survive.

00:17:00.618 --> 00:17:01.953
(tense music)

